# Workbook concepts skill

The why behind the model: literate programming as the authoring paradigm, WebAssembly
as the universal render target, and why we author even our own docs as a workbook.
This skill grounds an agent in the rationale so its choices align with the model
rather than fight it.

When the user asks "why is it built this way" or needs the philosophy behind a
decision, load the references below.

app :workbook_concepts do
  title       "Workbook concepts"
  description "The rationale behind workbooks: literate programming, WebAssembly as render target, and docs-as-a-workbook. Use when explaining why the model works the way it does or making a design choice that should align with it."

  section "Foundations" do
    page "preface/literate-programming"
    page "preface/why-webassembly"
  end

  section "In practice" do
    page "blog/why-we-author-docs-as-a-workbook"
  end
end
